values ('e6f7a8b9-0c1d-4e21-8f30-4a5b6c7d8e11', 'lodging-hotel-operations', 'Lodging / Hotel Operations', 'This course prepares students to lead hotel rooms operations across the complete guest lifecycle. Students examine hotel ownership and affiliation, rooms-division organization, staffing and shift control, reservations and distribution, forecasting and inventory, front-office and guest-accounting processes, in-house service, housekeeping and laundry, service recovery, property technology, privacy and cybersecurity, night audit, performance metrics, quality assurance, safety and accessibility, facilities and sustainability, group and special-stay complexity, and cross-departmental decision making. A semester-long synthetic-property simulation integrates guest experience, employee well-being, operational control, asset care, and financial results.');

